ers their tracker as a trait, and track what controls do.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingFromViews":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingFromViews","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give views the tracker the way each framework passes values down, and let modifiers and controls track what views do."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/AutomaticTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/automatictracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/AutomaticTracking","title":"Automatic Tracking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Track screen views, control activations and the app’s lifecycle without a call at each place they happen."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding":{"url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding","identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding","title":"AmplitudeEncoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to an Amplitude project through its HTTP V2 API."}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/TrackingPlanWorkflow":{"title":"Exporting and Checking a Tracking Plan","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tell the people and services that read your events what each event holds, and hear about a change that would break their data before it ships."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingplanworkflow","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/TrackingPlanWorkflow"},"doc://EventMacros/documentation/EventMacros":{"title":"EventMacros","kind":"sy