ic"},"doc://AppKitTracking/documentation/AppKitTracking":{"url":"\/documentation\/appkittracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/AppKitTracking\/documentation\/AppKitTracking","title":"AppKitTracking","abstract":[{"text":"Let AppKit views find their tracker up the responder chain, and track what controls do.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftUITracking/documentation/SwiftUITracking":{"title":"SwiftUITracking","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Give SwiftUI views a tracker through the environment, and track what they do with view modifiers.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUITracking\/documentation\/SwiftUITracking"},"doc://Traffluent/documentation/Traffluent/ChangingEvents":{"url":"\/documentation\/traffluent\/changingevents","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","title":"Changing an Event","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An event’s version counts the changes that records stored before them can’t be read through, and only those. A compatible change keeps the version; a breaking one raises it."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://TrackingPlans/documentation/TrackingPlans":{"url":"\/documentation\/trackingplans","identifier":"doc:\/\/TrackingPlans\/documentation\/TrackingPlans","title":"TrackingPlans","abstract":[{"text":"Export every event an app tracks as JSON Schema that people and services outside the app can read, and check each change against the plan committed before it.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://GRDBPersistence/documentation/GRDBPersistence":{"title":"GRDBPersistence","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Keep each record in a table of the app’s own GRDB database until it is delivered.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/grdbpersistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GRDBPersistence\/document